weapon_keywords.Heavy:
In your Shooting phase, **add 1 to the hit roll** for each attack made with a **[HEAVY]** weapon if all of these apply to the attacking unit:

- it is **unengaged**;
- it was **not set up on the battlefield this turn**;
- **no model** in it has moved **more than 3"** this turn.

Standing still is no longer required — a 3" reposition keeps the bonus.

weapon_keywords.Scouts:
The ability always reads **Scouts X"**. In the **Resolve Pre-battle Abilities** step, if every model in a unit has it, you can pick **one** of these:

- if the unit is in **strategic reserves**, set it up anywhere wholly within your deployment zone;
- if the unit is wholly within your deployment zone, it makes a **scout move** of up to X";
- if it is embarked in a **Dedicated Transport** wholly within your deployment zone and every model aboard has Scouts, that transport makes the scout move.

A scout move must end more than **8" horizontally from all enemy units**.

Note the reserves option: a Scouts unit held back can deploy into your own zone instead of moving, which is new and easy to overlook.

weapon_keywords.Firing Deck:
Always written **Firing Deck X**. In your Shooting phase, each time this **Transport** is selected to shoot with units embarked inside it:

1. select up to **X** embarked models, excluding any whose unit has already shot this phase;
2. for each, select one of its ranged weapons, excluding **[ONE SHOT]** weapons;
3. until the Transport has resolved its attacks it counts as having those weapons **as well as** its own;
4. until the end of the turn, units embarked within it are **not eligible to shoot**.

So the passengers fire through the hull rather than shooting separately, and they give up their own shooting to do it.
